      "question": "My older emails show 0 opens. Is that a glitch?",
      "answer": "Almost always, no. Open tracking is opt-in, and it only applies to emails sent *after* you turn it on. If an email was sent before you enabled tracking — or while it was disabled — Buttondown never injected the tracking pixel, so there's nothing to count and it will show 0 opens forever. This is expected, and there's no way to retroactively add tracking to an email that's already been sent."
