      "question": "Why do my open numbers differ between views, or look low right after sending?",
      "answer": "Buttondown reports analytics in two places: the [Analytics page](https://buttondown.com/analytics), which aggregates across all your emails, and a specific email's analytics, which you reach from the `...` menu on a sent email. They measure the same things, but to keep the dashboard fast some figures are cached — the number you see is a recent snapshot rather than a live query.\n\nTwo consequences follow. First, the recipient count shown in the confirmation box right after you send is an in-progress figure that rises as the send completes and as delivery and bounce receipts come back, so it can look low at first. Second, a metric can briefly differ between a specific email's analytics and the main Analytics page, because the per-email view may be serving a slightly older cached value. In both cases the cache catches up on its own — if a number looks off, the first thing to try is checking again a little later."
